<Base title="About" description="Who writes here.">
	<div class="page about-grid">
		<div class="slot">your photo<br />portrait &middot; 5:6</div>
		<div>
			<h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
			<p>
				Placeholder prose in your voice, not lorem ipsum &mdash; two or three paragraphs on what you
				do, what you keep failing at, and why any of this is on the internet.
			</p>
			<p>
				Then one paragraph that isn&rsquo;t about work, because the people who actually read an about
				page are looking for that one.
			</p>
			<dl class="facts">
				<dt>Based</dt>
				<dd>Somewhere with decent coffee</dd>
				<dt>Doing</dt>
				<dd>Backend engineering</dd>
				<dt>Site</dt>
				<dd>Astro, no tracking, no cookie banner</dd>
			</dl>
		</div>
	</div>
	<div class="page page-body"></div>
</Base>
